    "content": "The tax deadline for those who filed an extension is October 15. This is the last day to submit your federal tax return (Form 1040) for the tax year if you filed an extension by April 15, though any taxes owed were still due by April 15. Key Details: Extension Filing: If you filed an extension (using Form 4868) by April 15, you have until October 15, 2026, to file your return. Payment Deadline: An extension gives you more time to file, not more time to pay. Taxes owed are still due by April 15. Disaster Areas: Taxpayers in specific federally declared disaster areas may have longer deadlines. Other Deadlines: Always check if Oct 15 falls on a weekend; however, for 2026, it is a Thursday. Ensure you complete your filing on the IRS website by this date to avoid failure-to-file penalties. IRS website",
